### 6. ELIGIBILITY AND INCLUSION/EXCLUSION CRITERIA BUILDER

Develop a standardized eligibility-rule generation engine.

Generate an editable eligibility matrix covering:

| Criterion | Inclusion requirements | Exclusion requirements | Guidance | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Research focus | Topic-relevant evidence | Outside research scope | Define topical boundaries | Pending |
| Population/problem | Eligible target | Irrelevant target | Follow framework | Pending |
| Intervention/exposure | Relevant intervention or exposure | Irrelevant intervention | Follow research questions | Pending |
| Outcomes | Relevant outcomes | Unrelated outcomes | Define measurable indicators | Pending |
| Geographic scope | Eligible locations | Outside specified scope | Define geographical boundaries | Pending |
| Publication period | Approved years | Outside period | Record date restrictions | Pending |
| Study design | Eligible designs | Ineligible designs | Specify study types | Pending |
| Publication type | Eligible original studies | Excluded publication types | Distinguish original research and reviews | Pending |
| Language | Approved languages | Unavailable languages | State limitations | Pending |
| Full-text availability | Applicable access requirements | Unavailable full text, if exclusion is justified | Record reasons | Pending |

The actual criteria must be generated from the research topic and approved methodology, not copied blindly from this example.

Support flexible inclusion and exclusion rules.

Generate standardized full-text exclusion reasons compatible with PRISMA reporting.

Examples include:

- Wrong research focus.
- Ineligible population or study area.
- Ineligible intervention or exposure.
- Irrelevant outcome.
- Ineligible study design.
- Wrong publication type.
- Outside publication period.
- Duplicate publication.
- Full text unavailable, where justified by the protocol.

Preserve the specific exclusion reason for each excluded full-text report.

