### 15. PROTOCOL VERSIONING, APPROVAL AND CHANGE MANAGEMENT

Implement a formal protocol version management system.

Every protocol must have:

- Unique protocol identifier.
- Associated research project.
- Version number.
- Creation date.
- Last modification date.
- Author or responsible researcher.
- Approval status.
- Methodological framework.
- Version history.
- Change summary.

Support protocol statuses:

- Draft.
- Under review.
- Needs revision.
- Approved.
- Superseded.
- Archived.

After approval, protocol modifications must create a new version rather than silently changing the approved version.

Record:

- Modified section.
- Previous content.
- Revised content.
- Reason for modification.
- Modification date.
- Responsible user.
- Approval status.

Where appropriate, record the date and justification of protocol amendments.

Preserve the original approved protocol for auditability and reproducibility.

