### 21. STRICT DEVELOPMENT RULES

1. Do not replace existing functional components unnecessarily.
2. Do not disrupt existing research projects or databases.
3. Do not silently modify approved protocol sections.
4. Do not fabricate references, DOI numbers, search results, or publication statistics.
5. Do not fabricate database retrieval counts.
6. Do not confuse generated search strategies with executed searches.
7. Do not treat PRISMA reporting guidelines as review conduct methodologies.
8. Do not treat quality appraisal instruments as reporting guidelines.
9. Do not recommend statistical meta-analysis without evaluating feasibility.
10. Do not present AI-generated recommendations as researcher-approved decisions.
11. Do not automatically apply protocol amendments to previous screening decisions.
12. Do not claim validation or testing without evidence.
13. Maintain backward compatibility with existing modules.
14. Preserve protocol history and research audit trails.

